    "lawCode": "Amd §170, Dom Rel L",
    "lawSection": "Domestic Relations Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S169\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the domestic relations law, in relation to grounds for\nan action for divorce\n\n\n SUMMARY :\nThis bill would add a new subdivision 7 to section 170 of the domestic\nrelations law. This bill would allow that an action for divorce may be\nmaintained by a husband or wife to procure a judgement divorcing the\nparties and dissolving the parties and dissolving the marriage upon\nfinal conviction of a class A felony; and/or a class B or C violent\nfelony as defined in section 70.02 of the penal law; and/or the final\nconviction of the defendant for a felony sex offense as defined in\narticle one hundred thirty of the penal law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nGrounds for divorce in New York are purely statutory.  The grounds in\nwhich a divorce may be granted have not been expanded since 1966.\nUnder current law, a spouse may file for divorce on the ground of\nimprisonment, only after their spouse has been imprisoned for three\nyears. This provision would allow the non imprisoned spouse the option\nof filing for divorce upon the defendant spouse's conviction of the\naforementioned felony offense(s).\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATION :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
